Two bugs cause blue freeze:

1. `THREE.Timer` not update in [src/scene.js](file:///home/gaitano/01-studio/01-src/shaders-intro-01/src/scene.js#L73-L76). `THREE.Timer` require `timer.update()` call per frame. Without call, `timer.getElapsed()` always return 0. Also `getElapsed()` return total time, not delta — use `=`, not `+=`.
2. Time scale wrong in [src/shader/fragment.glsl](file:///home/gaitano/01-studio/01-src/shaders-intro-01/src/shader/fragment.glsl#L12). `getElapsed()` return seconds, not milliseconds. Dividing by 1000 make 1 cycle take ~16 minutes. Look static blue.

Fix [src/scene.js](file:///home/gaitano/01-studio/01-src/shaders-intro-01/src/scene.js#L73-L76):

```javascript
function render() {
  timer.update();
  uniforms.u_time.value = timer.getElapsed();
  renderer.render(scene, camera);
}
```

